<html>

<head>
    <style>
        @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
            body {
                background: #333;
                color: white;
            }
            a {
                color: skyblue;
            }
        }
        .container {
            font-family: sans-serif;
            max-width: 800px;
            margin: 0 auto;
        }
        .intro {
            text-align: center;
        }
        .licenses-list {
            list-style-type: none;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
        }
        .license-used-by {
            margin-top: -10px;
        }
        .license-text {
            max-height: 200px;
            overflow-y: scroll;
            white-space: pre-wrap;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>
    <main class="container">
        <div class="intro">
            <h1>Third Party Licenses</h1>
            <p>This page lists the licenses of the projects used in mdoc.</p>
            <p>presidio-analyzer 0.1.11: Copyright (c) 2026 presidio-rust contributors.
                Licensed under the MIT terms below; the complete upstream notice is
                retained in resources/presidio-license.txt.</p>
        </div>

        <h2>Attribution</h2>
        <p>mdoc is a modified version of <a href="https://github.com/packetThrower/zorite">Zorite</a>,
            originally developed by packetThrower (Will Lehnertz) and contributors.
            Copyright &copy; 2026 packetThrower / Zorite contributors; copyright &copy; 2026
            lawkitt / mdoc contributors for modifications. The application is licensed under
            the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later, without warranty. The crates in
            crates/ retain their MIT licenses and original copyright notices in each crate's
            LICENSE file.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Vendored GPUI Linux renderer: Zed, Apache-2.0, with Zorite's combining-mark
                correction; see vendor/gpui-pre-wgpu/ZORITE-PATCH.md.</li>
            <li>Text recognition: the MIT-licensed pdf-inspector fork, OAR/PaddleOCR models
                (Apache-2.0), and separately downloaded PDFium and ONNX Runtime. Setup installs
                their licenses and notices under mdoc/ocr/v1/licenses.</li>
            <li>Pseudonymization: gliner2-rs 0.9.6 by Dario Finardi, published by Jugaad s.r.l.
                (Apache-2.0); license and NOTICE in resources/gliner2-license.txt and
                resources/gliner2-notice.txt. The optional GLiNER2 privacy PII model
                (Apache-2.0) is installed with its model card, attribution and Microsoft MIT
                terms. No model weights are distributed with mdoc.</li>
            <li>Spellcheck: unmodified Hunspell dictionaries from LibreOffice: en_US (SCOWL by
                Kevin Atkinson; affix file by Geoff Kuenning, BSD-style), en_GB (LGPL; David
                Bartlett, Brian Kelk, Andrew Brown and Marco A.G. Pinto) and ru_RU
                (BSD-style, &copy; 1997&ndash;2008 Alexander I. Lebedev). Notices are in
                crates/mdoc-spell/dictionaries/.</li>
            <li>Test fixtures retain their notices in tests/fixtures/import/README.md and
                tests/fixtures/import/LICENSE.anydoc. The synthetic OCR qualification fixtures
                are CC0-1.0.</li>
            <li>README images: the Word screenshot shows the UK Model Services Contract, Crown
                copyright, under the Open Government Licence v3.0; the scanned page is from the
                public-domain opinion Brown v. Board of Education, 347 U.S. 483 (1954); the
                Apple icon is from Simple Icons (CC0 1.0).</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Overview of licenses:</h2>
        <ul class="licenses-overview">
            {{#each overview}}
            <li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> ({{count}})</li>
            {{/each}}
        </ul>

        <h2>All license text:</h2>
        <ul class="licenses-list">
            {{#each licenses}}
            <li class="license">
                <h3 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h3>
                <h4>Used by:</h4>
                <ul class="license-used-by">
                    {{#each used_by}}
                    <li><a href="{{#if crate.repository}} {{crate.repository}} {{else}} https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}} {{/if}}">{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</a></li>
                    {{/each}}
                </ul>
                <pre class="license-text">{{text}}</pre>
            </li>
            {{/each}}
        </ul>
    </main>
</body>

</html>
